' 6. Daily review (spaced repetition)
' Use case: Daily review (Practice) · Actor: Learner
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Repository: srs.repository.ts (cards, reviews), XP and achievement repositories
'   - Unit of work: grading a card (lock card → schedule → save card + review → streak day) is one transaction
'     (services/srs.service.ts reviewCard → withTransaction)
'   - Observer: the level-up notification is published to every open tab (realtime.service.ts publish)
'   - Chain of responsibility: authenticate middleware before every request (note)
'   - Decorator: action() wraps every controller (note)
'   Worth a note, not a pattern: the SM-2 scheduler (learning/srsScheduler.ts) is a pure domain function, with no
'   database or clock inside it.
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 06 Daily review
title 6. Daily review (spaced repetition)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Learner
boundary "Web app" as Web
control "SRS controller" as Ctrl
control "SRS service" as Svc
control "SRS scheduler\n(SM-2)" as Sched
control "Gamification\nservice" as Gam
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
control "Notification\n(realtime)" as Notif

note over Web, Ctrl : «Chain of responsibility»: headers → CORS → authenticate → controller\n«Decorator»: action() wraps every controller (error handling)
note over Repo : «Repository»\nall SQL lives here

Learner -> Web : Open Daily review
Web -> Ctrl : GET /api/units
Ctrl --> Web : units (finished lessons)

opt finished lessons changed since last time
  Web -> Ctrl : POST /api/srs/cards (words + kanji)
  Ctrl -> Svc : enrollItems()
  Svc -> Repo : insertCards()
  Repo -> DB : INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
  Ctrl --> Web : { added }
end

Web -> Ctrl : GET /api/srs/queue
Ctrl -> Svc : getQueue()
Svc -> Repo : listDueCards() + listNewCards(5 a day)
Repo -> DB : SELECT (hidden cards left out)
Ctrl --> Web : cards
Web --> Learner : first card

loop each card in the session
  Learner -> Web : Show answer, grade (Again / Hard / Good / Easy)

  alt grade the card
    Web -> Ctrl : POST /api/srs/reviews (card, grade)
    Ctrl -> Svc : reviewCard()

    group «Unit of work» withTransaction(): all or nothing
      Svc -> Repo : findCardForUpdate()
      Repo -> DB : SELECT … FOR UPDATE
      Svc -> Sched : scheduleReview(card, grade, now)
      Sched --> Svc : next interval, ease, due date
      Svc -> Repo : saveReview()
      Repo -> DB : UPDATE card, INSERT review
      Svc -> Repo : recordActivity() (streak day)
    end

    Svc -> Gam : rewardActivity("review")
    Gam -> Repo : awardXP (2 XP, daily limit 60)
    Gam -> Repo : check achievements
    opt level up
      Gam -> Notif : notifyLevelUp()
      Notif -> DB : save notification
      Notif --> Web : publish → bell updates (all open tabs)
      note right of Notif : «Observer»\npublish() → every open tab\nis subscribed
    end
    Gam --> Svc : reward
    Ctrl --> Web : next due date + reward
    Web --> Learner : "+XP" pop-up, next card
    opt graded Again
      Web -> Web : card added again at the end of the session
    end

  else hide the card instead
    Learner -> Web : Hide it
    Web -> Ctrl : PATCH /api/srs/cards/:type/:id { suspended: true }
    Ctrl -> Svc : setCardSuspended()
    Svc -> Repo : setSuspended()
    Repo -> DB : UPDATE suspended_at
    Web --> Learner : next card
  end
end

Web --> Learner : "All done for today"

opt cards due within 24 h
  Learner -> Web : Review ahead
  Web -> Ctrl : GET /api/srs/queue?ahead=1
  Ctrl -> Svc : getQueue({ ahead: true })
  Ctrl --> Web : cards due soon
  note over Learner, Web : Same loop as above, reviews sent with **ahead: true**
end
@enduml
